            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="0956" n="836" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg836"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1/343: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva
                        (Gilbert)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-11-16T16:00:00-05:00">November 16,
                            1932—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>33. For Davis. Your 40, November 15th 3 P.M. The President is to confer with Mr.
                    Roosevelt within near future as to Economic Conference. Suggest, if possible,
                    postponing decision as to time of Conference until that meeting.</p>
                <pb facs="0957" n="837" xml:id="pg837"/>
                <p>While appreciating certain advantages of delaying until April or May do not wish
                    to decide yet definitely against early meeting which might be of benefit to the
                    world and which apparently is much favored by British. Will wire further as soon
                    as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
